@ cases.a-proof-that-uses-a-function-that-runs-as-written-says-why-0.diagnostics[]
file = "input/main.taut"
name = "shown"
message = "`show_path` is not defined in proofs: it runs as written and is not checked by the kernel, because it uses `Text::of_nat`, which runs as written: it is a built-in of the prelude; it is in the standard library: `import std::Text`; a proof uses only what the kernel checked; when a kernel declaration of that name was meant, import it where the name is written: a name a macro's `quote` writes means what the macro's own file sees"
span = " «show_path»("

